findings.what:
Live, no-reflash control surface that already reaches the boards. Two families.
(a) Composed-scene fields 45–63 per board (scene, widths, travel, separation, quiet, return, trail, trips, feathers, recovery, choreography, initiator, answer delay, phrase, ml_target, quiet_scope), wire profile 6.
(b) In-house path controls read every frame:
- mode (32/18/8/7/11);
- palette;
- speed → motion_scale = speed×2;
- mirror;
- per-board response gain 0–2, which multiplies peak_scaled, vu_level, vu_average and observed_peak_scaled before the clamps;
- per-board Mood (atlas already notes Mood).

River Surge build→cut detector, inside the K1/DualMCU product effect catalogue.
- fast envelope τ 0.5 s, slow envelope τ 20 s, peak envelope τ 4 s;
- 'build' is remembered for 2 s when fast/slow > 1.3;
- fires when fast < 0.45 × peak, with a 4 s refractory;
- spawns an outward wavefront from the centre (speed 2.5× drift, life 0.8 s, half-width 3 px).
It detects the fall after a build: the cut, not the drop.

OnsetBeat (production K1_ONSET_V2):
- log-magnitude positive spectral flux over bins 1–76 (transient), 1–25 (kick), 25–50 (snare), 70–80 (hi-hat);
- 14-frame median ×1.6 + 0.05 adaptive threshold;
- peak picking (pre-max 4, wait 4) and per-band refractory (6 / 5 / 3 frames);
- monotonic event IDs per class, decaying levels, IOI beat-lock tail (300–1000 ms, half / double alias).
It is wrapped in AudioPipeline and published into AudioFeaturesV1 event flags and IDs.

MusicalSaliency and ChordDetect.
MusicalSaliency has four axes:
- harmonic (chord-root change → 1.0, type change → 0.6);
- rhythmic (beat confidence or novelty change);
- timbral (|Δ novelty| / 0.05);
- dynamic (|Δ spectral energy| / 0.02).
Each axis has asymmetric rise / fall smoothing (0.15/0.8, 0.05/0.3, 0.1/0.5, 0.08/0.4 s), and they combine into weighted overall saliency with an adaptive floor and a salient event.
ChordDetect is stateless K1_CHORD_V2 over a 12-bin chroma: type, root, confidence, and root / third / fifth strengths.

Multi-candidate tempo field (TempoFieldV1 plus TempoPhaseTracks):
- up to 8 candidates (BPM bins separated by 6 %), each with salience, phase01 from correlation over the stored novelty ring, phase uncertainty, beat index and Q32 period;
- admission states fresh / coasting (≤ 48,000 frames) / stale (96,000);
- generation IDs and support intervals;
- fields for derived ratio candidates (root_id, ratio_numerator / denominator, derived) and a deriveTempoPhase(p/q) helper.
Plus composed_timing::Clock: candidate selection over the donor 96 tempi with challenger dwell 600 / 800 ms and ≥ 8 samples, phase slew ≤ 20 % of oscillator speed, 1.5 s coasting and boundary pulses.

In-house v8 family modes at 160 px, beside v9's 32 / 18:
- mode 8 Waveform (displacement × sensitivity, photons gain);
- mode 7 Fast;
- mode 11 Waveform Hybrid, which draws an oscilloscope-like shape from the 4×96 PCM history radially from the centre.
Colour comes from familyColour (FastLED 16-slot compiled palettes).

Existing per-board darkness / gate telemetry in the status JSON:
- in-house: render_us, generation, capture_us, fresh, source_silence, raw_rms, quiet_entry_rms, admission open, peak_stage1, position, deposit_strength, injection_count;
- plus inhouse_donor_peak_squared;
- donor: the BLM1 64-record bloom trace (valid / admission flags, peak, floor, raw / conditioned VU, feed).
